course: dictionary
lesson: 8095
title: Remote, far away and more
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Remote means far away. A remote place is far from towns, shops and other people. «They camped on a remote common far from habitations.» A common is open land that anyone may use, and habitations means houses, so the campers were somewhere with no houses nearby.
explain: The word has other meanings too. It can mean far away in time, as in the remote past, or a very small chance, as in a remote chance. It can even describe a person who seems distant and unfriendly. The words around it show you which meaning fits.
explain: A remote control is a small device that works a TV or toy from a distance. «Drive a remote-control car only in the yard, park or a quiet path, never in the street.» Test your meaning by swapping it in: far away, or small, or distant, and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Remote means far away from towns and other people.
fact: Remote can also mean far away in time, like the remote past.
fact: A remote is a small device that controls a TV or toy from a distance.
fact: A remote chance is a very small chance.
fact: Some children in remote areas learn online, which is called remote learning.
exercise: «They camped on a remote common far from habitations.» What does remote mean here? | Very loud and busy | Close to the shops | *Far away from towns and other people | Very old
exercise: Mia says a remote-control car is safe to drive in the street. What should she do instead? | Let it run after her into traffic | Drive it fast in the street | Drive it in the street at night | *Drive it only in the yard, a park or a quiet path
exercise: Ben says his chance of winning is remote. What does remote chance mean? | *A very small chance | A chance to be on TV | A chance to go on a holiday | A chance that happens every day
test: Which phrase means far away in time? | a remote area | a remote control | a remote chance | *the remote past
test: What is a remote? | A kind of TV show | A type of battery | A far-off island | *A small device that controls a TV or toy from a distance
exam: Which meaning fits best? «She gave him a remote reply, as if she did not want to talk.» | *Distant and unfriendly, not warm | A very small chance | Far away in time | A small device
